    "name": "colorwheel",
    "description": "Show what ColorWheel draws; progress plays a demo of the progress row; invert switches limits between used and left",
    "argumentHint": "[progress|invert]",
    "output": "# ColorWheel\n\nReplies in the desktop app keep the app's own typography: **bold**, *italic*, `inline code`, [links](https://github.com/AlexeyHRDesign) and tables that wrap to the chat width.\n\n| Element | Drawn as | Theme |\n|---|---|---|\n| Text, lists, tables | the app's markdown | light and dark |\n| Code | the app's code view | light and dark |\n| Alerts | cards | one tone for both |\n| Mermaid | full-width SVG | switches with the app |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Diagrams have **Open large** for a zoomable view and **Copy source** for the mermaid code.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Ask Claude for a flow or a chart and it will reach for mermaid.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> The terminal keeps Claude Code's own renderer.\n\n```ts\nexport const greet = (name: string) => `hello, ${name}`\n```\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  R[Reply] --> S{Split}\n  S -->|text| M[Markdown]\n  S -->|code| C[Code view]\n  S -->|mermaid| D[Diagram]\n```\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant U as You\n  participant C as Claude\n  participant W as ColorWheel\n  U->>C: prompt\n  C->>W: markdown\n  W-->>U: themed reply\n```\n\n```mermaid\nxychart-beta\n  title \"Reply render time, ms\"\n  x-axis [Text, Table, Code, Diagram]\n  y-axis \"ms\" 0 --> 450\n  bar [410, 260, 190, 150]\n  line [180, 120, 95, 80]\n```"
   }
  ],
